  "worked_solution": "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\nv={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the inverse of $T$:\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{(5)(1)-(6)(2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo the original vector is\n\n$$\nv=-\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12}{7} \\\\ \\frac{4}{7}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
